    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81acbdca_d5f85b70",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T23:08:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like whole point here is to set flags in this hook handler so that they are passed to cpufreq_update_util(..) at line 1090. I agree with Greg this could be done inside your vendor code where this hook handler stores the flag value in some internal state.\n\nThe flags are consumed in `cpufreq_update_util(..)`\u0027s call of `data-\u003efunc` which is setup by your cpufreq governor via `cpufreq_add_update_util_hook(..)`. I believe this is in your version of the schedutil governor, correct?\n\nSo, can\u0027t this patch be reduced to just the invocation of this hook here and at line 1385.",
      "revId": "61814ef31ff3a8ab13e4c1a8bf86d6271ab787ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce9b60da_27f56d2b",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1105075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T23:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rick, can we add a vendor task_struct attribute to mark it.",
      "parentUuid": "81acbdca_d5f85b70",
      "revId": "61814ef31ff3a8ab13e4c1a8bf86d6271ab787ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57a2c638_c778f336",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324603
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-15T00:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I actually thought about it, but I\u0027m worrying about some race condition may corrupt the flag value - 2 rt tasks are enqueued to the same cpu at the same time, which is rare but theoretically could happen.",
      "parentUuid": "ce9b60da_27f56d2b",
      "revId": "61814ef31ff3a8ab13e4c1a8bf86d6271ab787ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5214ed7_10f752b1",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-15T15:58:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couldn\u0027t you handle that case by storing the passed-in task_struct associated with the flags? Then the flags are a per-waking-task instead of per-current-cpu. Anyway, it seems like this race can be handled in the vendor code and doesn\u0027t need the interface changes here.",
      "parentUuid": "57a2c638_c778f336",
      "revId": "61814ef31ff3a8ab13e4c1a8bf86d6271ab787ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21abfecc_6e75e658",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1367,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324603
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-16T02:25:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand your point, the purpose here is to update the flags based on the task property. The difficulty is that when cpufreq_update_util(struct rq *rq, unsigned int flags) is called, which goes to the update function of governor, it has no info about which task it is updating, so the best chance is to store the flags in per-cpu level, but it may have issue as mentioned. I agreed it\u0027s better not to update the API if possible, maybe I could try upstream first. Thanks :)",
      "parentUuid": "b5214ed7_10f752b1",
      "revId": "61814ef31ff3a8ab13e4c1a8bf86d6271ab787ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
